<article class="env-theorem" id="86BA8F">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/86BA8F">Theorem <span data-tag="86BA8F">3.2.0.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a simplicial set, $\calC $ a simplicial category, and $\phi : \sCoNerve [S] \rightarrow \calC ^{op}$ a functor between simplicial categories. Then there exists a pair of adjoint functors </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix {(\mSet )_{/S} \ar @< .4ex>[r]^{ St^{+}_{\phi }} &amp;  (\mSet )^{\calC } \ar @< .4ex>[l]^{Un^{+}_{\phi }}}  \]
</div>
  <p> with the following properties: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
The functors $(St^{+}_{\phi }, Un^{+}_{\phi })$ determine a Quillen adjunction between $(\mSet )_{/S}$ (with the Cartesian model structure) and $(\mSet )^{\calC }$ (with the projective model structure). 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
If $\phi $ is an equivalence of simplicial categories, then $(St^{+}_{\phi }, Un^{+}_{\phi })$ is a Quillen equivalence. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof of Theorem <a href="/tag/86BA8F" data-tag="86BA8F">3.2.0.1</a>.</strong>
       For each simplicial set $S$, let $(\mSet )^{\sCoNerve [S]^{op}}_{f}$ denote the category of projectively fibrant objects of $(\mSet )^{\sCoNerve [S]^{op}}$, and let $W_{S}$ be the class of weak equivalences in $( \mSet )^{\sCoNerve [S]^{op}}_{f}$. Let $W'_{S}$ be the collection of pointwise equivalences in $(\mSet )_{/S}^{\circ }$. We have a commutative diagram of simplicial categories 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { ((\mSet )^{\sCoNerve [S]^{op}})^{\circ } \ar [r]^{ Un^{+}_{S} } \ar [d] &amp;  (\mSet )_{/S}^{\circ } \ar [d]^{\psi _{S}} \\ ( \mSet )^{\sCoNerve [S]^{op}}_{f}[W_{S}^{-1} ] \ar [r]^{\phi _ S} &amp;  ( \mSet )_{/S}^{\circ }[ {W'}^{-1}_{S} ] } \]
</div>
    <p>
       (see Notation <a href="/tag/" data-tag="">None</a>). In view of Lemma <a href="/tag/EC884A" data-tag="EC884A">3.2.4.1</a>, it will suffice to show that the upper horizontal map is an equivalence of simplicial categories. Lemma <a href="/tag/" data-tag="">None</a> implies that the left vertical map is an equivalence. Using Lemma <a href="/tag/8CBA0B" data-tag="8CBA0B">2.2.3.6</a> and Remark <a href="/tag/" data-tag="">None</a>, we deduce that the right vertical map is also an equivalence. It will therefore suffice to show that $\phi _{S}$ is an equivalence. 
    <p>
      Let $\calU $ denote the collection of simplicial sets $S$ for which $\phi _{S}$ is an equivalence. We will show that $\calU $ satisfies the hypotheses of Lemma <a href="/tag/DA0877" data-tag="DA0877">2.2.3.5</a>, and therefore contains every simplicial set $S$. Conditions $(i)$ and $(ii)$ are obviously satisfied, and condition $(iii)$ follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/EC884A" data-tag="EC884A">3.2.4.1</a> and Proposition <a href="/tag/64A540" data-tag="64A540">3.2.3.4</a>. We will verify condition $(iv)$; the proof of $(v)$ is similar. 
    <p>
      Applying Corollary <a href="/tag/" data-tag="">None</a>, we deduce: 
    <p>
      <ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(\ast )$"><p>
The functor $S \mapsto ( \mSet )^{\sCoNerve [S]^{op}}_{f} [W_ S^{-1}]$ carries homotopy colimit diagrams indexed by a partially ordered set to homotopy limit diagrams in $\sCat $. 
</p>
</li>
</ul>
    <p>
      Suppose given a pushout diagram 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { X \ar [r] \ar [d]^{f} &amp;  X' \ar [d] \\ Y \ar [r] &amp;  Y' } \]
</div>
    <p>
       in which $X, X', Y \in \calU $, where $f$ is a cofibration. We wish to prove that $Y' \in \calU $. We have a commutative diagram 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { ( \mSet )^{\sCoNerve [Y']^{op}}_{f}[W_{Y'}^{-1}] \ar [dr]^{\phi _{Y'}} &amp;  &amp;  \\ &amp;  (\mSet )_{/Y'}^{\circ }[ {W'}_{Y'}^{-1}] \ar [r]^{u} \ar [d]^{v} \ar [dr]^{w} &amp;  (\mSet )_{/Y}^{\circ }[ {W'}_{Y}^{-1}] \ar [d] \\ &amp;  (\mSet )_{/X'}^{\circ }[ {W'}_{X'}^{-1}] \ar [r] &amp;  (\mSet )_{/X}^{\circ }[ {W'}_{X}^{-1} ]} \]
</div>
    <p>
       Using $(\ast )$ and Corollary <a href="/tag/" data-tag="">None</a>, we deduce that $\phi _{Y'}$ is an equivalence if and only if, for every pair of objects $x,y \in (\mSet )_{/Y'}^{\circ }[ {W'}_{Y'}^{-1}]$, the diagram of simplicial sets 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { \bHom _{ (\mSet )_{/Y'}^{\circ }[ {W'}_{Y'}^{-1}] }( x, y) \ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  \bHom _{ (\mSet )_{/Y}^{\circ }[ {W'}_{Y}^{-1}] }( u(x), u(y) ) \ar [d] \\ \bHom _{ (\mSet )_{/X'}^{\circ }[ {W'}_{X'}^{-1}] }( v(x), v(y) ) \ar [r] &amp;  \bHom _{ (\mSet )_{/X}^{\circ }[ {W'}_{X}^{-1}] }( w(x), w(y) ) } \]
</div>
    <p>
       is homotopy Cartesian. Since $\psi _{Y'}$ is a weak equivalence of simplicial categories, we may assume without loss of generality that $x = \psi _{Y'}( \overline{x} )$ and $y = \psi _{Y'}( \overline{y} )$, for some $ \overline{x}, \overline{y} \in (\mSet )^{\circ }_{/Y'}$. It will therefore suffice to prove that the equivalent diagram 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { \bHom ^{\sharp }_{ Y' }( \overline{x}, \overline{y}) \ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  \bHom ^{\sharp }_{Y }( \overline{u}(\overline{x}), \overline{u}(\overline{y}) ) \ar [d] \\ \bHom ^{\sharp }_{ X' }( \overline{v}(\overline{x}), \overline{v}(\overline{y}) ) \ar [r]^{g} &amp;  \bHom ^{\sharp }_{X }( \overline{w}(\overline{x}), \overline{w}(\overline{y}) ) } \]
</div>
    <p>
       is homotopy Cartesian. But this diagram is a pullback square, and the map $g$ is a Kan fibration by Lemma <a href="/tag/E975E4" data-tag="E975E4">3.2.4.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>